  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Q1456939/relation1841167 identifies three separated archaeological areas, not a solid building. Seven individual pinned PMTiles column footprints determine the standing row. Its own measured map axis controls the internal architecture, rather than applying the broad precinct bounding-box axis to every shaft. Eight small eastern mapped remnants are low fragment treatments. Native+X east/+Z south and runtime heading0. Only the visible western court has an authored ground surface. Other archaeological boundary polygons do not imply invented building masses or paved platforms. Later neighboring footprints stay independent.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Two ordinary current-state photographs guide approximate shafts6.8m tall above the white bases, a1.35m stepped stylobate and low0.35–2.2m broken walls. No capitals/entablature are invented. Fallen drums, paving patches, low court rectangles, small fragment height and erosion are picture-led visualization estimates, not surveyed inventories."
  },
